  "scope": "Opt-in combined Rust service candidate: declared union166, capture-capable inventory163; public Record Clip retains its exact Take without claiming the public Start Take lease. Public manual Restore retains the sole snapshot owner and closed eight-mutation batch custody through settlement with strict metadata-only v3 receipts. Stream effects remain excluded from immutable Take/media configurations. Default178 and compatibility116 unchanged. Combined source/package qualification is recorded separately.",
  "policy": {
    "sourceFiles": "Every src/**/*.ts file is explicitly classified below. Production and tests are hashed separately by role; tests do not establish native runtime ownership.",
    "nativeFiles": "Every project-owned native/src/**/*.rs, native/tests/**/*.rs and optional native/build.rs plus Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and rust-toolchain.toml is hash-bound at seal. Dependency .cargo-home caches and target output are excluded. Inline cfg(test) modules are hashed but excluded from the narrow production placeholder check.",
    "routing": "Each manifest tool is explicitly native-readonly, native-local, native-readonly-workflow or compat. Requests and closed implemented-handler maps define admission; adopting route changes requires --update --adopt-manifest-routes after review. TS remains compatibility authority even where native read-only request execution duplicates a narrow slice.",
    "evidence": "A seal detects drift and inventory omissions; it does not prove semantic parity, absence of all stubs, performance, delivered packaging, or native OBS behavior. Required differential and package checks remain separate.",
    "manualSnapshots": "Opt-in LIST/CAPTURE and manual RESTORE; caller policy precedes snapshot selection including dryRun, missing selection stays offline, and valid selection is rechecked by the combined Service. Manual restore uses only the eight closed legacy snapshot mutations, one SerialRealtime nonhalting batch, strict complete-vector v3 receipts and no lifecycle/file/Stop authority. Unknown outcomes never authorize replay. The sole snapshot history owner is retained through actual publication and admitted restore planning/settlement. Snapshots are ordered observations, not an atomic OBS transaction or Stage receipt. Missing/replaced established history, corrupt JSON, unproven locks, unsafe paths, byte capacity and publication uncertainty refuse explicitly. Native never renames corrupt history away or steals an old lock based on age; these are conservative differences from the predecessor. Source read-only classification permits capture during a take; snapshot file publication borrows no recording receipt writer. The default owner caps history at 8 MiB and concrete capture at 4096 requests per batch, with the Service absolute deadline. Blocking filesystem calls are joined; a deadline does not prove a hard kernel-I/O latency bound.",
    "propertyEnumeration": "Dedicated guarded adapter only; absent from RawReadRequest. Reported source kind governs the exact predecessor guard; ScreenCaptureKit display_uuid/application always refuse and XComposite capture_window requires a nonempty string, while integer window properties skip the unsafe settings probe. Native additionally refuses changed canonical evidence at actual dispatch/result publication, without retry. Optional nullable arrays of record items preserve every valid response field; malformed shapes reproduce Source SDK output-validation messages within a 32 KiB diagnostic limit, above which native refuses explicitly."
  },
